# i18n readability follow-up (named constants, worked examples)

Context: A readability review of the English/Korean UI internationalisation
found raw DOM node-type numbers, an unnamed cookie lifetime, a fallback chain
in translateWith without examples, an implicit else branch in the mutation
observer, and an environment variable read twice. No behaviour change.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/js/i18n.js
   Node.ELEMENT_NODE / TEXT_NODE / DOCUMENT_NODE / DOCUMENT_FRAGMENT_NODE
   instead of raw numbers (read only inside DOM functions, so the node test
   harness still works); ONE_YEAR_SECONDS for the ob_lang cookie max-age;
   one input -> output example per translateWith fallback branch; explicit
   characterData / attributes branch in observe(); keep-in-sync comment
   pointing to dependencies.py.
2. src/front/fastapi/dependencies.py
   ONTOBRICKS_UI_LANG read once into _ENV_UI_LANG; keep-in-sync comment
   pointing to i18n.js.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/global/js/i18n.js
- src/front/fastapi/dependencies.py

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/units/front`
-> 1074 passed; node --check i18n.js OK.
